  "description": "25X1A 25X1A Approved ForlWease 200, 1A -RDP78B0476 '630802 November 10, 1969 DECLASS REVIEW BY NrMA / DoD 25X1A 25X1A 25X1A To: From: Subject: Bi-Monthly Status REport No. 3 under This bi-monthly status report covers the period from August 22 through October 21, 1969. During this period two trips were made to the Customer's facility, as follows: September 8, 1969: This trip was concerned with,a review of both the philosophy, and a preliminary outline, of the handbook. October 21-22, 1969: This trip was concerned with delivery and review of three items; a detailed outline and chapters 1 and 2 of the handbook. Also, a complete chronological record of \"message traffic\". for'both.\"C\" and \"G.\" was finalized for inclusion in the handbook. Trip reports covering each trip have been submitted. During this period work has been concentrated on Chapter 1 and 2 of the handbook, from the standpoint of both content and format. The proposed handbook will not be a \"cookbook\", but will provide a technological basis for under- standing the image evaluation process in terms of its component parts and their inter-relationships. It will also establish those areas of evaluation which require further investigation. iff 7 F.XCL.U1 .U i RJ!.4 ABU MPJAT1G il;WNGRAQING AN ppro ed For Release 20 THIS M 9TEalA1 ^n, ^ T IA-RD `'-rs~' WITHIN THE MEANING 0 WTHIN THE OF THE ESPIONAGE LAAS, TITLE 18, USE, S\"CS. 793 /;N,} 794 THE TRANSMi;SiON OR REVELATION OF WHICH IN ANI MANNER TO AN UN IQ non.? - AUTHOR7t11 Pi RSCN Approved Fort/ lease 2005/02/ 7,:;:C1A-RDP78B0476 003000100 ) 1A The primary emphasis during the coming period will be on Chapter 3. It will be attempted in Chapter 3 to define, in terms of flow charts and descriptive material, the sequence of event and techniques which constitute image evaluation. Approvee r1 Aele4se 2005/02/17 : C1A-RDP78B0474A000300010022-2",
